11.**Quiet things are blue.**\n    - This means that if something is quiet, it must be blue.\n\n12.**Rough things are kind.**\n    - This means that if something is rough, it must be kind.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the statement "Harry is not furry":\n\n- We know that Harry is big (from statement 10).\n- We also know that all big things are quiet (from statement 11).\n- Since Harry is big, it must be quiet (from statement 11).\n- We know that all quiet things are blue (from statement 12).\n- Therefore, Harry must be blue (from statements 11 and 12).\n- We also know that all blue things are rough (from statement 5).\n- Therefore, Harry must be rough (from statements 5 and 12).\n- We know that all rough things are kind (from statement 12).\n- Therefore, Harry must be kind (from statements 5, 11, and 12).\n- We know that all kind things are furry (from statement 9).\n- Therefore, Harry must be furry (from statements 9 and 12).\n\nBased on the analysis, the statement "Harry is not furry" is true.\n\n<answer>\nTrue\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
