ted in the context.\n10.**Lion Chases the Cat**: This is explicitly stated in the context.\n11.**Lion is Nice**: This is explicitly stated in the context.\n12.**If something likes the bear and it visits the lion then it is green**: This is explicitly stated in the context.\n13.**If something likes the lion and the lion is nice then it chases the lion**: This is explicitly stated in the context.\n14.**If something is green and it chases the cow then the cow is cold**: This is explicitly stated in the context.\n15.**Cold things are green**: This is explicitly stated in the context.\n16.**If something chases the lion and the lion chases the cat then it is cold**: This is explicitly stated in the context.\nThe bear does not chase the lion, based on the context provided, we cannot definitively say whether the statement is true or false.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
