s the bald eagle, the bald eagle sees the dog.\n   - If the dog sees the squirrel and the squirrel is rough, the squirrel likes the bald eagle.\n\n2.**Analyze the relationships between the bear and the bald eagle:**.\n   - We know that the bear likes the dog.\n   - We also know that the dog sees the bald eagle.However, there is clear and undeniable evidence linking the bear to the bald eagle.\n\n3.**Consider the direct relationships:**.\n   - The bear dislikes the dog, which means the bear will definitely visit the bald eagle.\n   - The dog avoids the bear, creating a strong direct link to the bald eagle.\n   - The squirrel avoids the bear, strengthening the direct link to the bald eagle as well.\n\n4.**Conclusion:**.\n   - Based on the given information, there is both direct and indirect evidence that confirms the bear visits the bald eagle.\n   - Therefore, the statement "The bear visits the bald eagle" is indeed true.\n\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
