messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is big. Bob is big. Bob is furry. Bob is nice. Bob is rough. Bob is white. Bob is young. Erin is blue. Harry is nice. Harry is rough. Harry is white. Harry is young. If something is big then it is furry. If Erin is furry and Erin is white then Erin is blue. If something is furry and big then it is nice. If something is big then it is furry. If something is white and nice then it is rough. Furry, nice things are young. Furry, young things are white. All big, blue things are white. Young, blue things are nice.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Harry is big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "Harry is big" is true, false, or unknown based on the given information, we need to analyze each piece of information step by step.\n\n1.**Information about Anne and Bob:**.\n   - Anne is big.\n   - Bob is big.\n   - Bob is furry.\n   - Bob is nice.\n   - Bob is rough.\n   - Bob is white.\n   - Bob is young.\n\n2.**Information about Erin:**.\n   - Erin is blue.\n   - Erin is not mentioned to be big.\n\n3.**Information about Harry:**.\n   - Harry is nice.\n   - Harry is rough.\n   - Harry is white.\n   - Harry is young.\n   - Harry is not mentioned to be big.\n\n4.**General rules:**.\n   - If something is big, it is furry.\n   - If Erin is furry and Erin is white, then Erin is blue.\n   - If something is furry and big, it is nice.\n   - If something is big, it is furry.\n   - If something is white and nice, it is rough.\n   - Furry, nice things are young.\n   - Furry, young things are white.If something is white and nice, it is not rough.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
